## To release a new version, edit the version in the two lines below and nothing else.
## |cRRGGBB...|r in Title and Author colours them in the in-game add-on list; the version
## is read back through that markup, so it can sit inside or outside the colour.
## Title: |cFF69B4PB’s Translate|r 1.4.0-dev
## Author: |cFF69B4PinkBanther|r
## Description: Shows a Japanese translation under English chat messages -- your own and other players'. Translation runs entirely inside the add-on, with a built-in dictionary of everyday English, chat shorthand, ESO terms and Cyrodiil PvP calls and a small grammar that reorders English into Japanese, so the result is a rough literal rendering. /jp <text> translates a line for you alone; /pbtr add english = 日本語 adds your own words.
## Version: 1.4.0-dev
## APIVersion: 101050 101051
## OptionalDependsOn: LibHarvensAddonSettings>=20106 LibGroupBroadcast
## SavedVariables: PBsTranslate_Data

lang/strings.lua
lang/$(language).lua

Conjugate.lua
Lexicon.lua
Tokenizer.lua
Grammar.lua
Semantic.lua
Syntax.lua
SyntaxGen.lua
JaToEn.lua

dict/Core.lua
dict/Nouns.lua
dict/Adjectives.lua
dict/Verbs.lua
dict/Expressions.lua
dict/ESO.lua
dict/Cyrodiil.lua
dict/Irregular.lua

Main.lua
Settings.lua
Outgoing.lua
ShareSession.lua
Sharing.lua

